A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

<Callout kind="warn">
The historical policy below conflicts with the executable cause checks and the
[review of #4471](/kb/incidents/4471-split). It needs a support-desk decision.
[Proposed decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) describes merging by supported cause;
decision 0001 remains unchanged as the accepted historical record.
</Callout>

## Historical subject-only rule

A report is a duplicate when its **subject line matches** the subject of an open ticket
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):

1. lowercase the subject and strip punctuation;
2. look for an open ticket with the same subject;
3. found one: merge the report into it. None: open a new ticket.

<Callout>
Matching on subject is fast and needs no reading. During an incident that matters more than
anything else.
</Callout>

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Merge. Splitting a ticket later is cheaper than two engineers chasing the same bug.
